urname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>Cellular pathology of Niemann-Pick type C disease.</article-title><source>Semin Cell Dev Biol</source><volume>15</volume><fpage>445</fpage><lpage>454</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15207834</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Maxfield1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Maxfield</surname><given-names>FR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tabas</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2005</year><article-title>Role of cholesterol and lipid organization in disease.</article-title><source>Nature</source><volume>438</volume><fpage>612</fpage><lpage>621</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16319881</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Vanier1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vanier</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Millat</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Niemann-Pick disease type C.</article-title><source>Clin Genet</source><volume>64</volume><fpage>269</fpage><lpage>281</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12974729</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Puri1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Puri</surname><given-names>V</given-names></name><name><surname>Watanabe</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Dominguez</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Sun</surname><given-names>X</given-names></name><name><surname>Wheatley</surname><given-names>CL</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Cholesterol modulates membrane traffic along the endocytic pathway in sphingolipid-storage diseases.</article-title><source>Nat Cell Biol</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>386</fpage><lpage>388</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10559968</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Leventhal1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Leventhal</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Chen</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Tall</surname><given-names>AR</given-names></name><name><surname>Tabas</surname><given-names>I</given-names></name></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Acid sphingomyelinase-deficient macrophages have defective cholesterol trafficking and efflux.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>276</volume><fpage>44976</fpage><lpage>44983</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11579092</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Desnick1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Desnick</surname><given-names>RJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Schuchman</surname><given-names>EH</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Enzyme replacement and enhancement therapies: lessons from lysosomal disorders.</article-title><source>Nat Rev Genet</source><volume>3</volume><fpage>954</fpage><lpage>966</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12459725</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Sturley1"><label>18</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Sturley</surname><given-names>SL</given-names></name><name><surname>Patterson</surname><given-names>MC</given-names></name><name><surname>Balch</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Liscum</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name></person-group><year>2004</year><article-title>The pathophysiology and mechanisms of NP-C disease.</article-title><source>Biochim Biophys Acta</source><volume>1685</volume><fpage>83</fpage><lpage>87</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15465429</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Simons1"><label>19</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Simons</surname><given-names>K</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Jamming the endosomal system: lipid rafts and lysosomal storage diseases.</article-title><source>Trends Cell Biol</source><volume>10</volume><fpage>459</fpage><lpage>462</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11050411</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Koh1"><label>20</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Koh</surname><given-names>CH</given-names></name><name><surname>Cheung</surname><given-names>NS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2006</year><article-title>Cellular mechanism of U18666A-mediated apoptosis in cultured murine cortical neurons: bridging Niemann-Pick disease type C and Alzheimer's disease.</article-title><source>Cell Signal</source><volume>18</volume><fpage>1844</fpage><lpage>1853</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16797161</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Aniento1"><label>21</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Aniento</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Emans</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Griffiths</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Gruenberg</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Cytoplasmic dynein-dependent vesicular transport from early to late endosomes.</article-title><source>J Cell Biol</source><volume>123</volume><fpage>1373</fpage><lpage>1387</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8253838</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Fivaz1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Fivaz</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Vilbois</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Thurnheer</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Pasquali</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Abrami</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Differential sorting and fate of endocytosed GPI-anchored proteins.</article-title><source>EMBO J</source><volume>21</volume><fpage>3989</fpage><lpage>4000</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12145200</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Liscum1"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liscum</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Faust</surname><given-names>JR</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>The intracellular transport of low density lipoprotein-derived cholesterol is inhibited in Chinese hamster ovary cells cultured with 3-beta-&#x0005b;2-(diethylamino)ethoxy&#x0005d;androst-5-en-17-one.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>264</volume><fpage>11796</fpage><lpage>11806</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2745416</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000851-Kobayashi1"><label>24</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Kobayashi</surname><given-names>T</given-names></name><name><surname>Beuchat</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Lindsay</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Frias</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Palmiter</surname><given-names>RD</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Late endosomal membranes rich in lysobisphosphatidic acid regulate cholesterol transport.</article-title><source>Nat Cell Biol</source><volume>1</volume><fpage>113</fpage><lpage>118</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10559883</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone